2Co 8:1 , He stirs them up to a liberal contribution for the poor saints at Jerusalem, by the example of the Macedonians;
2Co 8:7 , by commendation of their former forwardness;
2Co 8:9 , by the example of Christ;
2Co 8:14 , and by the spiritual profit that shall redound to themselves thereby;
2Co 8:16 , commending to them the integrity and willingness of Titus, and those other brethren, who upon his request, exhortation, and commendation, were purposely come to them for this business.
